> Degeneracies and a rounded-product counterexample

Empty input returns empty. One distinct point returns one; two distinct points
use the historical lexicographic shortcut, which need not put the lowest-y point
first. At least three collinear distinct points are scanned and reduce to the
pivot and farthest endpoint. An edge-interior point is omitted. Exact duplicate
equality merges signed zeros, preserving the first matching original
representation.

For a rounding witness, set \(\varepsilon=2^{-52}\), \(a=(0,0)\),
\(b=(1,1+\varepsilon)\), \(c=(1+\varepsilon,1+2\varepsilon)\). All coordinates
are representable, and the exact determinant is

$$\Delta(a,b,c)=1+2\varepsilon-(1+\varepsilon)^2=-\varepsilon^2<0.$$
\alttext(The exact orientation is negative epsilon squared, although the two nearly equal products round to the same double value.)

The old rounded cross product returns zero here. Exact-sign sorting and scan
tests retain all three noncollinear vertices. Inputs at the subnormal and
maximum finite scales also require exact predicates; the core supports them,
while a display renderer has a narrower range and should not be used to certify
hull correctness.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/graham_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const double eps = std::ldexp(1., -52);
    const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> near{{0, 0}, {1, 1 + eps},
                                                  {1 + eps, 1 + 2 * eps}};
    const double rounded = dm::geometry::cross(near[0], near[1], near[2]);
    const int exact = dm::geometry::orientation_sign(near[0], near[1], near[2]);
    std::print("Rounded determinant: {}; exact sign: {}.\n\n", rounded, exact);
    const std::vector<std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D>> cases{
        {}, {{0, 0}, {-0., 0}}, {{2, -1}, {0, 4}},
        {{0, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, 2}, {1, 1}},
        {{0, 0}, {2, 0}, {2, 2}, {0, 2}, {1, 0}}, near
    };
    const std::vector<std::string> names{"empty", "duplicate point",
                                         "two-point shortcut", "collinear",
                                         "edge point", "near collinear"};
    std::vector<double> x, h;
    std::print("| case | original rows | distinct | hull vertices | first original row |\n| --- | ---: | " "---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < cases.size(); ++i) {
        const auto a = dm::geometry::graham_scan_analyze(cases[i]);
        x.push_back(i + 1);
        h.push_back(a.hull.size());
        std::print("| {}: {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i + 1, names[i],
                   cases[i].size(), a.work.distinct_points, a.hull.size(),
                   a.input_indices.empty() ? "none"
                   : std::to_string(a.input_indices[0]));
    }
    const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> tiny{{0, 0}, {4, 0}, {3, 1},
                                                  {4, 4}, {0, 4}};
    const auto t = dm::geometry::graham_scan_trace(tiny);
    bool quota = false, invalid = false;
    try {
        (void) dm::geometry::graham_scan_trace(tiny, {5, t.events.size() - 1});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        quota = true;
    }
    auto bad = tiny;
    bad.push_back({std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(), 0});
    try {
        (void) dm::geometry::graham_scan_trace(bad, {1, 1});
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        invalid = true;
    }
    const auto full =
        dm::geometry::graham_scan_trace(tiny, {5, t.events.size()});
    auto copy = full;
    copy.events[0].point = 99;
    std::print("\nOne-short event cap rejects: {}; exact cap retains {} events; nonfinite input rejected " "before caps: {}; copied history independent: {}.\n",
               quota, full.events.size(), invalid,
               full.events[0].point != copy.events[0].point);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.bars(x, h, "native hull size", {37, 99, 235}).title(
        "Degenerate inputs return points or a segment").x_label(
        "case: 1 empty; 2 duplicate; 3 pair; 4 line; 5 edge; 6 near").y_label(
        "strict hull vertices").y_limits(0, 5.4).save_svg(
        "build/graham_controls.svg");
    if (rounded != 0 || exact != -1 || h.back() != 3 || !quota || !invalid)
        throw std::runtime_error("boundary witnesses");
}
```
